(1099657, 134005, 19828, '<td valign="top">Gorgeous.<br/>8</td>', 'Gorgeous.8', '2005-01-10 10:06:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(1099658, 134789, 9939, '<td valign="top">The short definition of Bokeh from KenRockwell.com, that I am using for this challenge:  "Bokeh describes the rendition of out-of-focus points of light." Here we aren''t seeing so much points of light as just an out of focus background. Is the subject enhanced by the bokeh of the background? Somewhat. On the whole however this image doesn''t grab me.</td>', 'The short definition of Bokeh from KenRockwell.com, that I am using for this challenge:  "Bokeh describes the rendition of out-of-focus points of light." Here we aren''t seeing so much points of light as just an out of focus background. Is the subject enhanced by the bokeh of the background? Somewhat. On the whole however this image doesn''t grab me.', '2005-01-10 10:07:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(1099659, 134589, 9939, '<td valign="top">The short definition of Bokeh from KenRockwell.com, which I am using for voting on this challenge: "Bokeh describes the rendition of out-of-focus points of light."We are seeing that here.  Is the subject enhanced by the bokeh of the background? Yes- an interesting shot with a cool bluish feel.</td>', 'The short definition of Bokeh from KenRockwell.com, which I am using for voting on this challenge: "Bokeh describes the rendition of out-of-focus points of light."We are seeing that here.  Is the subject enhanced by the bokeh of the background? Yes- an interesting shot with a cool bluish feel.', '2005-01-10 10:08:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(1099660, 134771, 19828, '<td valign="top">I like this image a whole bunch.<br/>I am personnally a huge fan of selective desaturation.<br/>Therefore I gave you a 9.</td>', 'I like this image a whole bunch.I am personnally a huge fan of selective desaturation.Therefore I gave you a 9.', '2005-01-10 10:09:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(1099661, 133636, 9939, '<td valign="top">The short definition of Bokeh from KenRockwell.com, which I am using for voting on this challenge: "Bokeh describes the rendition of out-of-focus points of light." We are seeing only a little bokeh here.  Is the subject enhanced by the bokeh of the background? To me, not really.</td>', 'The short definition of Bokeh from KenRockwell.com, which I am using for voting on this challenge: "Bokeh describes the rendition of out-of-focus points of light." We are seeing only a little bokeh here.  Is the subject enhanced by the bokeh of the background? To me, not really.', '2005-01-10 10:10:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(1099663, 134590, 9939, '<td valign="top">The short definition of Bokeh from KenRockwell.com, which I am using for voting on this challenge: "Bokeh describes the rendition of out-of-focus points of light." To me this image does not show bokeh well at all.  Is the subject enhanced by the bokeh of the background? Based on the previous statement, no. Lovely roses though.</td>', 'The short definition of Bokeh from KenRockwell.com, which I am using for voting on this challenge: "Bokeh describes the rendition of out-of-focus points of light." To me this image does not show bokeh well at all.  Is the subject enhanced by the bokeh of the background? Based on the previous statement, no. Lovely roses though.', '2005-01-10 10:11:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(1099664, 134794, 9939, '<td valign="top">The short definition of Bokeh from KenRockwell.com, which I am using for voting on this challenge: "Bokeh describes the rendition of out-of-focus points of light." We do see some of that here. Is the subject enhanced by the bokeh of the background? Most definitely. A very beautiful image.</td>', 'The short definition of Bokeh from KenRockwell.com, which I am using for voting on this challenge: "Bokeh describes the rendition of out-of-focus points of light." We do see some of that here. Is the subject enhanced by the bokeh of the background? Most definitely. A very beautiful image.', '2005-01-10 10:12:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(1099665, 134718, 9939, '<td valign="top">The short definition of Bokeh from KenRockwell.com, which I am using for voting on this challenge: "Bokeh describes the rendition of out-of-focus points of light. We do see that here. " Is the subject enhanced by the bokeh of the background? Yes. However, this photo doesn''t make me go "wow".</td>', 'The short definition of Bokeh from KenRockwell.com, which I am using for voting on this challenge: "Bokeh describes the rendition of out-of-focus points of light. We do see that here. " Is the subject enhanced by the bokeh of the background? Yes. However, this photo doesn''t make me go "wow".', '2005-01-10 10:13:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(1099667, 133966, 9939, '<td valign="top">The short definition of Bokeh from KenRockwell.com, which I am using for voting on this challenge: "Bokeh describes the rendition of out-of-focus points of light." We see that here, though it is quite subtle. Is the subject enhanced by the bokeh of the background? Somewhat- the bokeh is so subtle as to make any sort of relationship impossible to discern. The colors are complimentary, however.</td>', 'The short definition of Bokeh from KenRockwell.com, which I am using for voting on this challenge: "Bokeh describes the rendition of out-of-focus points of light." We see that here, though it is quite subtle. Is the subject enhanced by the bokeh of the background? Somewhat- the bokeh is so subtle as to make any sort of relationship impossible to discern. The colors are complimentary, however.', '2005-01-10 10:15:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(1099668, 133846, 9939, '<td valign="top">The short definition of Bokeh from KenRockwell.com, which I am using for voting on this challenge: "Bokeh describes the rendition of out-of-focus points of light." Is the subject enhanced by the bokeh of the background? Definitely. Very nice.</td>', 'The short definition of Bokeh from KenRockwell.com, which I am using for voting on this challenge: "Bokeh describes the rendition of out-of-focus points of light." Is the subject enhanced by the bokeh of the background? Definitely. Very nice.', '2005-01-10 10:15:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(1099669, 134815, 9939, '<td valign="top">The short definition of Bokeh from KenRockwell.com, which I am using for voting on this challenge: "Bokeh describes the rendition of out-of-focus points of light." Is the subject enhanced by the bokeh of the background? Yep. Looks cold from front to back!</td>', 'The short definition of Bokeh from KenRockwell.com, which I am using for voting on this challenge: "Bokeh describes the rendition of out-of-focus points of light." Is the subject enhanced by the bokeh of the background? Yep. Looks cold from front to back!', '2005-01-10 10:15:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(1099672, 134403, 9939, '<td valign="top">The short definition of Bokeh from KenRockwell.com, which I am using for voting on this challenge: "Bokeh describes the rendition of out-of-focus points of light." We see that here, though it is quite subtle. Is the subject enhanced by the bokeh of the background? Somewhat. But any relationship between the foreground and background  is impossible to discern.</td>', 'The short definition of Bokeh from KenRockwell.com, which I am using for voting on this challenge: "Bokeh describes the rendition of out-of-focus points of light." We see that here, though it is quite subtle. Is the subject enhanced by the bokeh of the background? Somewhat. But any relationship between the foreground and background  is impossible to discern.', '2005-01-10 10:17:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(1099674, 134701, 9939, '<td valign="top">The short definition of Bokeh from KenRockwell.com, which I am using for voting on this challenge: "Bokeh describes the rendition of out-of-focus points of light." We sort of see that here. Mainly we see just an out of focus background. Is the subject enhanced by the bokeh of the background? Not really. If there is a relationship between the front and back it is impossible to discern.</td>', 'The short definition of Bokeh from KenRockwell.com, which I am using for voting on this challenge: "Bokeh describes the rendition of out-of-focus points of light." We sort of see that here. Mainly we see just an out of focus background. Is the subject enhanced by the bokeh of the background? Not really. If there is a relationship between the front and back it is impossible to discern.', '2005-01-10 10:18:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(1099675, 133344, 9939, '<td valign="top">The short definition of Bokeh from KenRockwell.com, which I am using for voting on this challenge: "Bokeh describes the rendition of out-of-focus points of light." We don''t really see points of l ight here in any form.  Is the subject enhanced by the bokeh of the background? Based on that definition, no.</td>', 'The short definition of Bokeh from KenRockwell.com, which I am using for voting on this challenge: "Bokeh describes the rendition of out-of-focus points of light." We don''t really see points of l ight here in any form.  Is the subject enhanced by the bokeh of the background? Based on that definition, no.', '2005-01-10 10:19:36.000000', NULL, 1),
