(1106443, 134211, 4285, '<td valign="top">Very rich colours but I think you have too much going on in the image which in and of itself is very distracting. I think the red/purple leaves against green grass is very appealing but you need to eliminate some of the other elements in your composition. Hope this is helpful.</td>', 'Very rich colours but I think you have too much going on in the image which in and of itself is very distracting. I think the red/purple leaves against green grass is very appealing but you need to eliminate some of the other elements in your composition. Hope this is helpful.', '2005-01-13 18:11:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(1106465, 133120, 4285, '<td valign="top">I think the idea of bokeh is to isolate the subject from the background by making it ( the background) so out of focus that it is unrecognizable and therefore not a distracting element in the image.  In this image, even though the fence is your subject, the eye is drawn to the much larger, more interesting mill.  Hope this is helpful.</td>', 'I think the idea of bokeh is to isolate the subject from the background by making it ( the background) so out of focus that it is unrecognizable and therefore not a distracting element in the image.  In this image, even though the fence is your subject, the eye is drawn to the much larger, more interesting mill.  Hope this is helpful.', '2005-01-13 18:20:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(1106469, 133694, 4338, '<td valign="top">good out of focus area, i had to lauh at this one because i shot  a starbucks cup ust like this but did not use it or the challene</td>', 'good out of focus area, i had to lauh at this one because i shot  a starbucks cup ust like this but did not use it or the challene', '2005-01-13 18:23:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(1106474, 134014, 4285, '<td valign="top">The idea of bokeh, as I understand it, is to separate the subject from the background, by making it (the background) out of focus to the point where it is unrecognizable, and therefore not distracting. Your title suggests the boy as your subject, but you focus on the toy.  And to add to that the BG isn''t out of focus enough to be considered bokeh. Hope this is helpful.</td>', 'The idea of bokeh, as I understand it, is to separate the subject from the background, by making it (the background) out of focus to the point where it is unrecognizable, and therefore not distracting. Your title suggests the boy as your subject, but you focus on the toy.  And to add to that the BG isn''t out of focus enough to be considered bokeh. Hope this is helpful.', '2005-01-13 18:26:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(1106488, 134608, 4285, '<td valign="top">You have created bokeh but the harsh flash on the ornament takes away from the image. Maybe try using natural or ambient light with a slower shutter or difusing your flash with tissue paper or the like. Hope this helps.</td>', 'You have created bokeh but the harsh flash on the ornament takes away from the image. Maybe try using natural or ambient light with a slower shutter or difusing your flash with tissue paper or the like. Hope this helps.', '2005-01-13 18:31:16.000000', NULL, 1),
