(1108930, 134797, 32122, '<td valign="top">This picture emits a feel of anticipation of sunshine</td>', 'This picture emits a feel of anticipation of sunshine', '2005-01-15 11:55:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(1108982, 134352, 31155, '<td valign="top">I love this shot!  It reminds me so much of home. (Australia)  I love the clarity in the foreground with the out of focus background, it really brings out the wild look of the Kookaburra.  You did really well with this category.</td>', 'I love this shot!  It reminds me so much of home. (Australia)  I love the clarity in the foreground with the out of focus background, it really brings out the wild look of the Kookaburra.  You did really well with this category.', '2005-01-15 12:52:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(1109026, 134605, 31213, '<td valign="top">Spooky...I can feel the energy!</td>', 'Spooky...I can feel the energy!', '2005-01-15 13:30:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(1109028, 133564, 31214, '<td valign="top">I love the colors.  This shot really stands out!</td>', 'I love the colors.  This shot really stands out!', '2005-01-15 13:31:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(1109030, 133948, 31214, '<td valign="top">Nicely represented.</td>', 'Nicely represented.', '2005-01-15 13:32:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(1109032, 133109, 31214, '<td valign="top">I love how you''ve captured a "roundness" theme....the droplets, the berry, the Bokeh circles.  Great job!</td>', 'I love how you''ve captured a "roundness" theme....the droplets, the berry, the Bokeh circles.  Great job!', '2005-01-15 13:33:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(1109033, 134695, 31214, '<td valign="top">Nicely done....great attention to Rule of Thirds too.</td>', 'Nicely done....great attention to Rule of Thirds too.', '2005-01-15 13:34:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(1109036, 134684, 31214, '<td valign="top">You have a nice shot here, but I think you would benefit by some composition improvements.  First, study the Rule of Thirds.  The head of your subject is smack dab in the middle.  You don''t want that.  In terms of the theme, you don''t seem to be getting enough Bokeh, shallow DOF.  Great use of lighting though.  Good luck!</td>', 'You have a nice shot here, but I think you would benefit by some composition improvements.  First, study the Rule of Thirds.  The head of your subject is smack dab in the middle.  You don''t want that.  In terms of the theme, you don''t seem to be getting enough Bokeh, shallow DOF.  Great use of lighting though.  Good luck!', '2005-01-15 13:36:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(1109050, 133891, 4517, '<td valign="top">One of my favorites.10. Well done.</td>', 'One of my favorites.10. Well done.', '2005-01-15 14:00:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(1109052, 134675, 4517, '<td valign="top">Great idea and perfect photo. Should ribbon. 10</td>', 'Great idea and perfect photo. Should ribbon. 10', '2005-01-15 14:01:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(1109053, 134771, 23394, '<td valign="top">interesting take on the challenge.  yes, you have created a bokeh effect, but, for me, it really isn''t enhancing the subject.  the blowouts in the liquid catch my eye first, then the effect of the selective desat is to take my eye straight down the image to the drop.  the way this is composed, it makes the viewing more of a rushed trip than a journey.  maybe that is what you intended.  i like the balance between the light and dark sides of the blade.  as far as images go, this is fine; as for the challenge, i don''t think this is the best your could have done for an entry.</td>', 'interesting take on the challenge.  yes, you have created a bokeh effect, but, for me, it really isn''t enhancing the subject.  the blowouts in the liquid catch my eye first, then the effect of the selective desat is to take my eye straight down the image to the drop.  the way this is composed, it makes the viewing more of a rushed trip than a journey.  maybe that is what you intended.  i like the balance between the light and dark sides of the blade.  as far as images go, this is fine; as for the challenge, i don''t think this is the best your could have done for an entry.', '2005-01-15 14:01:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(1109054, 134588, 4517, '<td valign="top">Very attractive and colourful image.10</td>', 'Very attractive and colourful image.10', '2005-01-15 14:02:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(1109055, 134546, 4517, '<td valign="top">Beautiful but the bokeh could be better, light a little distracting.7</td>', 'Beautiful but the bokeh could be better, light a little distracting.7', '2005-01-15 14:04:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(1109064, 133731, 23394, '<td valign="top">this is a strange composition, the juxtaposition of the oriental carving and the mystic bokeh.  here, the bokeh is as much the subject as is the carving, as opposed to being a subtle enhancer.  you are on the right track, i just think the image would have been a bit stronger if the dots of light were muted a bit.  also, the proximity to the carving and the way it fills the left side of the frame also gives a feeling of invasion of personal space, as if it''s too close to me, or i''m too close to it.  neither really works well if you are trying to convey a sense of meditation.</td>', 'this is a strange composition, the juxtaposition of the oriental carving and the mystic bokeh.  here, the bokeh is as much the subject as is the carving, as opposed to being a subtle enhancer.  you are on the right track, i just think the image would have been a bit stronger if the dots of light were muted a bit.  also, the proximity to the carving and the way it fills the left side of the frame also gives a feeling of invasion of personal space, as if it''s too close to me, or i''m too close to it.  neither really works well if you are trying to convey a sense of meditation.', '2005-01-15 14:20:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(1109068, 134003, 23394, '<td valign="top">very interesting image.  i think you are on the right track, and that this image has a lot of promise.  with a subject that small, it really needs to knock the viewer''s socks off when the image is this large; unfortunately, there are so many other elements in the image competing for attention that your single droplet starts to lose its strength.  with such very strong bokeh all the way through, you could actually crop this image in half and have something that absolutely rocked.  try it:  hold your left hand up to cover the whole left half of the image and you''ll see what i mean.  anyways, this is good work.  good luck!</td>', 'very interesting image.  i think you are on the right track, and that this image has a lot of promise.  with a subject that small, it really needs to knock the viewer''s socks off when the image is this large; unfortunately, there are so many other elements in the image competing for attention that your single droplet starts to lose its strength.  with such very strong bokeh all the way through, you could actually crop this image in half and have something that absolutely rocked.  try it:  hold your left hand up to cover the whole left half of the image and you''ll see what i mean.  anyways, this is good work.  good luck!', '2005-01-15 14:24:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(1109072, 134731, 23394, '<td valign="top">overall this is a nice image that meets the challenge well.  you could have done without the lights in the top right--they are more of a distraction than an enhancement to your image.  good job!</td>', 'overall this is a nice image that meets the challenge well.  you could have done without the lights in the top right--they are more of a distraction than an enhancement to your image.  good job!', '2005-01-15 14:26:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(1109074, 134734, 23394, '<td valign="top">great shot!  most excellent bokeh!  i''ll be surprised if this doesn''t make its way to the front page.</td>', 'great shot!  most excellent bokeh!  i''ll be surprised if this doesn''t make its way to the front page.', '2005-01-15 14:27:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(1109077, 134769, 23394, '<td valign="top">i like your idea, and hope that you will revisit it after the challenge.  as for this entry, i think the execution falls short and is not really doing what you want it to.  the focus is a bit soft, and the bokeh is too distracting.  actually, you have three background elements competing with each other as opposed to acting in support of your subject.  the glass behind the pitcher really needs to go, as do the lights back next to the window, as does the window, for that matter.  to get the viewer''s attention, you need to reduce the visual clutter that doesn''t contribute.  it also appears that you could use a bit more liquid in the decanter.   hope this helps.</td>', 'i like your idea, and hope that you will revisit it after the challenge.  as for this entry, i think the execution falls short and is not really doing what you want it to.  the focus is a bit soft, and the bokeh is too distracting.  actually, you have three background elements competing with each other as opposed to acting in support of your subject.  the glass behind the pitcher really needs to go, as do the lights back next to the window, as does the window, for that matter.  to get the viewer''s attention, you need to reduce the visual clutter that doesn''t contribute.  it also appears that you could use a bit more liquid in the decanter.   hope this helps.', '2005-01-15 14:32:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(1109081, 133201, 23394, '<td valign="top">i''m not quite sure what to make of your entry; it isn''t really moving me.  i think that your bokeh is a bit too strong and the shape of the leaf is a bit disconcerting.  on one hand, you have proven to yourself that you can capture a bokeh effect; now what you need to do put it to work to enhance your images.</td>', 'i''m not quite sure what to make of your entry; it isn''t really moving me.  i think that your bokeh is a bit too strong and the shape of the leaf is a bit disconcerting.  on one hand, you have proven to yourself that you can capture a bokeh effect; now what you need to do put it to work to enhance your images.', '2005-01-15 14:36:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(1109084, 134716, 21362, '<td valign="top">Oh my gosh, I''ve never seen anything like that. *shiver*</td>', 'Oh my gosh, I''ve never seen anything like that. *shiver*', '2005-01-15 14:39:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(1109090, 134797, 23394, '<td valign="top">this is an interesting composition that i feel would be stronger without the stem.  the bokeh is nice and well-rendered, contributing a smooth background for your leaf.  good work!</td>', 'this is an interesting composition that i feel would be stronger without the stem.  the bokeh is nice and well-rendered, contributing a smooth background for your leaf.  good work!', '2005-01-15 14:44:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(1109114, 134690, 23394, '<td valign="top">yes, you have achieved a bokeh effect...too bad your subject is not that interesting, at least in this composition.  simplicity is the key.  you want to get the viewer''s attention with something appealing.  even if you want to convey something like ice damage, if you work at it, you can find an artistic way to bring it across.  here, you probably could have succeeded if you had cropped the image down to the area near the intersection of the frond and the undamaged one (to me, that is the most interesting part of the entire image).  hope this helps some.</td>', 'yes, you have achieved a bokeh effect...too bad your subject is not that interesting, at least in this composition.  simplicity is the key.  you want to get the viewer''s attention with something appealing.  even if you want to convey something like ice damage, if you work at it, you can find an artistic way to bring it across.  here, you probably could have succeeded if you had cropped the image down to the area near the intersection of the frond and the undamaged one (to me, that is the most interesting part of the entire image).  hope this helps some.', '2005-01-15 14:57:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(1109119, 134301, 23394, '<td valign="top">in this image, the shallow dof really leaves me wanting.  there''s not enough in part that is sharp for me to latch on to.  this is more of an image that has some stuff razor sharp and a lot of stuff oof, and i can''t tell what you want me to look at, or what type of reaction you want me to have.  the bokeh is there, but it is not really doing anything to compensate for the blurry part of the subject.  sorry if this is harsh.</td>', 'in this image, the shallow dof really leaves me wanting.  there''s not enough in part that is sharp for me to latch on to.  this is more of an image that has some stuff razor sharp and a lot of stuff oof, and i can''t tell what you want me to look at, or what type of reaction you want me to have.  the bokeh is there, but it is not really doing anything to compensate for the blurry part of the subject.  sorry if this is harsh.', '2005-01-15 15:02:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(1109120, 134667, 25464, '<td valign="top">An appealing shot that meets the challenge well.  Good job.</td>', 'An appealing shot that meets the challenge well.  Good job.', '2005-01-15 15:02:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(1109121, 134650, 25464, '<td valign="top">This is a good demonstration of a linked background.  I think the color is a little flat and the straw needed to be in good focus.  Good idea.</td>', 'This is a good demonstration of a linked background.  I think the color is a little flat and the straw needed to be in good focus.  Good idea.', '2005-01-15 15:03:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(1109125, 134808, 23394, '<td valign="top">like i''m going to have anything bad to say about this guy...<br/> <br/>excellent portrait.  your bokeh, though, is a bit busy and distracting from an otherwise powerful image.  you would have done well, even if you had cropped off the left 20% of the image.  keep in mind, good bokeh enhances the subject; you could probably revisit this with some minor burning and have a killer image.  good luck!</td>', 'like i''m going to have anything bad to say about this guy... excellent portrait.  your bokeh, though, is a bit busy and distracting from an otherwise powerful image.  you would have done well, even if you had cropped off the left 20% of the image.  keep in mind, good bokeh enhances the subject; you could probably revisit this with some minor burning and have a killer image.  good luck!', '2005-01-15 15:05:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(1109127, 133762, 25464, '<td valign="top">I never knew what Witchhazel looked like.  Now I get the name.  I think this would have been improved if you had chosen a few blooms for subject and got closer.  The bloom out of focus in the upper right and the piece of bloom in the upper left corner are distracting.  The bokeh background is wonderfully done.  Good luck.</td>', 'I never knew what Witchhazel looked like.  Now I get the name.  I think this would have been improved if you had chosen a few blooms for subject and got closer.  The bloom out of focus in the upper right and the piece of bloom in the upper left corner are distracting.  The bokeh background is wonderfully done.  Good luck.', '2005-01-15 15:06:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(1109128, 133849, 23394, '<td valign="top">this is a beautiful image, and one of my favorites in the challenge.  excellent bokeh.  this image has the feeling of three kids, looking out the door, in anticipation of being told it''s ok to go on outside to play.  well done!</td>', 'this is a beautiful image, and one of my favorites in the challenge.  excellent bokeh.  this image has the feeling of three kids, looking out the door, in anticipation of being told it''s ok to go on outside to play.  well done!', '2005-01-15 15:07:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(1109131, 134775, 25464, '<td valign="top">ths is a really nice shot.  I would have liked a slightly tighter crop to eliminate the piece of bloom showing on the bottom and get a little closer to the subject.  I understand why you didn''t though the background is balanced perfectly with the darker shades of green in the lower right and the flash of yellow in the lower left.  Maybe a little closer and slightly downward to still capture those background elements.  Very nice job. 8.</td>', 'ths is a really nice shot.  I would have liked a slightly tighter crop to eliminate the piece of bloom showing on the bottom and get a little closer to the subject.  I understand why you didn''t though the background is balanced perfectly with the darker shades of green in the lower right and the flash of yellow in the lower left.  Maybe a little closer and slightly downward to still capture those background elements.  Very nice job. 8.', '2005-01-15 15:08:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(1109133, 134802, 25464, '<td valign="top">Not really my cup of tea, so I originally scored lower.  On second glance this is perfectly done.  Bumping up.</td>', 'Not really my cup of tea, so I originally scored lower.  On second glance this is perfectly done.  Bumping up.', '2005-01-15 15:09:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(1109136, 134672, 25464, '<td valign="top">Interesting composition.</td>', 'Interesting composition.', '2005-01-15 15:11:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(1109138, 134604, 25464, '<td valign="top">Interesting.  I think the subject is a bit too far away, and the fence (I am guessing) is a little distracting.  Nice bokeh.</td>', 'Interesting.  I think the subject is a bit too far away, and the fence (I am guessing) is a little distracting.  Nice bokeh.', '2005-01-15 15:13:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(1109140, 134687, 23394, '<td valign="top">interesting take on the challenge.  i love the mood you''ve created, but somehow, it feels a little flat, lacking warmth.  i also think the bottle could have been a big closer to the glass, and that the top of the bottle is a bit too close to the top of the frame.  you have done good work here, but, taking advantage of advanced editing rules can make whole point differences in these challenges.  i like the leg showing through the glass, but don''t like all the other distracting reflections in the glass.  it took a while for the glass beside the model to register with me; maybe a 1/3 to a 1/2 f-stop adjustment would have allowed the same background effect, but have brought her glass into the image a bit more.  cheers to taking a risk!  good luck!</td>', 'interesting take on the challenge.  i love the mood you''ve created, but somehow, it feels a little flat, lacking warmth.  i also think the bottle could have been a big closer to the glass, and that the top of the bottle is a bit too close to the top of the frame.  you have done good work here, but, taking advantage of advanced editing rules can make whole point differences in these challenges.  i like the leg showing through the glass, but don''t like all the other distracting reflections in the glass.  it took a while for the glass beside the model to register with me; maybe a 1/3 to a 1/2 f-stop adjustment would have allowed the same background effect, but have brought her glass into the image a bit more.  cheers to taking a risk!  good luck!', '2005-01-15 15:14:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(1109142, 134716, 23394, '<td valign="top">WHAT IS THAT?!?!?  i know there are a lot of things i haven''t seen before, and this is one of them.  wow.  you got my attention.  yes, you also have a bokeh effect, but it is a bit busy (a little burning and gaussian blur could help that, though).  normally, i''m not a big fan of centered subjects, but it works here.  good luck!</td>', 'WHAT IS THAT?!?!?  i know there are a lot of things i haven''t seen before, and this is one of them.  wow.  you got my attention.  yes, you also have a bokeh effect, but it is a bit busy (a little burning and gaussian blur could help that, though).  normally, i''m not a big fan of centered subjects, but it works here.  good luck!', '2005-01-15 15:17:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(1109144, 134733, 23394, '<td valign="top">nice, pleasant image with a good bokeh.  the colors are sublime, and the detail suberb.  i''m getting cold just looking at this!  good job, and good luck!</td>', 'nice, pleasant image with a good bokeh.  the colors are sublime, and the detail suberb.  i''m getting cold just looking at this!  good job, and good luck!', '2005-01-15 15:18:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(1109148, 134014, 23394, '<td valign="top">oh, how i can related to this!  great capture, interesting bokeh.</td>', 'oh, how i can related to this!  great capture, interesting bokeh.', '2005-01-15 15:19:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(1109149, 134515, 25464, '<td valign="top">I think this needed to be cropped in on the left to just outside the three aligned petals and just below that same lower petal eliminating the darker areas on the bottom.  Very nice shot though.</td>', 'I think this needed to be cropped in on the left to just outside the three aligned petals and just below that same lower petal eliminating the darker areas on the bottom.  Very nice shot though.', '2005-01-15 15:19:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(1109150, 133703, 23394, '<td valign="top">this makes me feel cold, just looking at it!  excellent work, nice bokeh!  good luck!</td>', 'this makes me feel cold, just looking at it!  excellent work, nice bokeh!  good luck!', '2005-01-15 15:20:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(1109153, 133027, 23394, '<td valign="top">while this image meets the challenge, i''m not quite sure what you are after with it.  it isn''t really grabbing me and moving me in anyway.  as i view it, i''m left feeling that you have shown me that you can technically produce bokeh, but i don''t feel that you are really doing anything with it.  sorry if this harsh.</td>', 'while this image meets the challenge, i''m not quite sure what you are after with it.  it isn''t really grabbing me and moving me in anyway.  as i view it, i''m left feeling that you have shown me that you can technically produce bokeh, but i don''t feel that you are really doing anything with it.  sorry if this harsh.', '2005-01-15 15:22:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(1109160, 134197, 23394, '<td valign="top">and you are appealing to my artistic side here (as opposed to my logical side...)?<br/> <br/>this is an interesting composition, if a bit busy in the background.  not really getting a feel for the relationship between your bokeh and the subject.  as for the subject, without the title, i would have no clue as to what i was looking at (well, maybe i''d guess a saw blade, but i''d still be wondering what is going on in the background).  you have proven that you can achieve bokeh, now you need to put it to work, to make it contribute to your images, rather than detract from them.  sorry if this is harsh, but that''s how i''m seeing your image.</td>', 'and you are appealing to my artistic side here (as opposed to my logical side...)? this is an interesting composition, if a bit busy in the background.  not really getting a feel for the relationship between your bokeh and the subject.  as for the subject, without the title, i would have no clue as to what i was looking at (well, maybe i''d guess a saw blade, but i''d still be wondering what is going on in the background).  you have proven that you can achieve bokeh, now you need to put it to work, to make it contribute to your images, rather than detract from them.  sorry if this is harsh, but that''s how i''m seeing your image.', '2005-01-15 15:25:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(1109165, 134338, 23394, '<td valign="top">very clever image.  really wild bokeh here, as well.  you probably could have titled it "ham-bo-ker"</td>', 'very clever image.  really wild bokeh here, as well.  you probably could have titled it "ham-bo-ker"', '2005-01-15 15:32:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(1109167, 134339, 23394, '<td valign="top">nice image, good detail.  little too much negative space on the right.  love the colors.  nice bokeh in support of your subject.  good work!</td>', 'nice image, good detail.  little too much negative space on the right.  love the colors.  nice bokeh in support of your subject.  good work!', '2005-01-15 15:33:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(1109171, 134701, 23394, '<td valign="top">yes, this makes me feel cold! from the looks of things, you probably would have had a stronger challenge entry if you had adjusted your angle slightly and cropped in on the center part of the post.  you are on the right track, just keep on working with it!</td>', 'yes, this makes me feel cold! from the looks of things, you probably would have had a stronger challenge entry if you had adjusted your angle slightly and cropped in on the center part of the post.  you are on the right track, just keep on working with it!', '2005-01-15 15:36:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(1109175, 134726, 23394, '<td valign="top">very wild image!  this is one of the most memorable images i''ve seen, just because of the colors.  great detail.  not thrilled about how centered the eye is (and that looks like something that could be strengthened by some judicious cropping).  all in all, i''ll be surprised if this doesn''t wind up on the front page!  good luck!</td>', 'very wild image!  this is one of the most memorable images i''ve seen, just because of the colors.  great detail.  not thrilled about how centered the eye is (and that looks like something that could be strengthened by some judicious cropping).  all in all, i''ll be surprised if this doesn''t wind up on the front page!  good luck!', '2005-01-15 15:40:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(1109190, 134705, 23394, '<td valign="top">this is an interesting image, but lacking any real sharpness.  the bokeh is nice, but not enough to compensate for all the oof subject matter.</td>', 'this is an interesting image, but lacking any real sharpness.  the bokeh is nice, but not enough to compensate for all the oof subject matter.', '2005-01-15 16:01:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(1109191, 134786, 23394, '<td valign="top">i''m sorry, but this image almost looks like a giant space alien ship about to eat some unsuspecting orator.  i am quite sure that is not what you intended, but that''s how it see it...</td>', 'i''m sorry, but this image almost looks like a giant space alien ship about to eat some unsuspecting orator.  i am quite sure that is not what you intended, but that''s how it see it...', '2005-01-15 16:03:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(1109192, 133344, 23394, '<td valign="top">sorry, but what you have here is a close up with a shallow dof, and that does not equate to bokeh.  this may work as a stock shot, but definitely not for this challenge.</td>', 'sorry, but what you have here is a close up with a shallow dof, and that does not equate to bokeh.  this may work as a stock shot, but definitely not for this challenge.', '2005-01-15 16:04:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(1109193, 134150, 23394, '<td valign="top">i admire your attempt, but feel that the execution is letting you down.</td>', 'i admire your attempt, but feel that the execution is letting you down.', '2005-01-15 16:05:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(1109197, 133636, 23394, '<td valign="top">this is an interesting image, but the shallow dof that is not really equating to bokeh.  i still like the image, and am adding it to my favorites, but am not finding it a good challenge entry.</td>', 'this is an interesting image, but the shallow dof that is not really equating to bokeh.  i still like the image, and am adding it to my favorites, but am not finding it a good challenge entry.', '2005-01-15 16:07:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(1109198, 134609, 23394, '<td valign="top">interesting take on the challenge.  will be very curious to see how this finishes up.  good luck.</td>', 'interesting take on the challenge.  will be very curious to see how this finishes up.  good luck.', '2005-01-15 16:08:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(1109201, 134635, 23394, '<td valign="top">interesting take on the challenge.  excellent capture of a stare.  will be interesting to see how this stacks up against the traditional bokeh shots.  good luck.</td>', 'interesting take on the challenge.  excellent capture of a stare.  will be interesting to see how this stacks up against the traditional bokeh shots.  good luck.', '2005-01-15 16:09:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(1109204, 134216, 23394, '<td valign="top">strange indeed.  i am always curious when i see shots like this, as to why i don''t take more risk.  i mean, really, to take a perfectly innocent piece of fruit and to run it through with 15-20 nails, then to shoot a macro with a blurry background.  keeping in mind that bokeh contributes and enhances, i''m not sure it that''s happening here, but i don''t think it really matters.</td>', 'strange indeed.  i am always curious when i see shots like this, as to why i don''t take more risk.  i mean, really, to take a perfectly innocent piece of fruit and to run it through with 15-20 nails, then to shoot a macro with a blurry background.  keeping in mind that bokeh contributes and enhances, i''m not sure it that''s happening here, but i don''t think it really matters.', '2005-01-15 16:14:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(1109206, 134805, 23394, '<td valign="top">this is some serious eye-candy.  the detail you have caught in the droplets is absolutely incredible.  i''ll be surprised if this isn''t on the front page when this is over.  good luck!</td>', 'this is some serious eye-candy.  the detail you have caught in the droplets is absolutely incredible.  i''ll be surprised if this isn''t on the front page when this is over.  good luck!', '2005-01-15 16:15:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(1109208, 134459, 23394, '<td valign="top">yes, you have captured an image of a shell on the beach, a very, very empty beach, at that.  while the background helps accentuate the emptyness of the beach, it is not what i would really consider a bokeh effect.</td>', 'yes, you have captured an image of a shell on the beach, a very, very empty beach, at that.  while the background helps accentuate the emptyness of the beach, it is not what i would really consider a bokeh effect.', '2005-01-15 16:17:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(1109209, 134127, 23394, '<td valign="top">ouch.  i''m not sure what you were after here.  this is interesting, but i don''t think it is much of a challenge entry.</td>', 'ouch.  i''m not sure what you were after here.  this is interesting, but i don''t think it is much of a challenge entry.', '2005-01-15 16:18:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(1109214, 134310, 23394, '<td valign="top">this is not what i''d really call a "challenge entry".  you have shot a less than interesting subject dead-on center.  the lighting looks under control, and the image is sharp enough under these conditions to indicate that you can do better...you just need to work on composition.  keep in mind, not every image is going to appeal to every viewer; the key is, though, to create images that will give people more reasons to want to look at them than to just pass them by.  and, when it comes to challenges, well, read scalvert''s thread about the recipe for ribboning...</td>', 'this is not what i''d really call a "challenge entry".  you have shot a less than interesting subject dead-on center.  the lighting looks under control, and the image is sharp enough under these conditions to indicate that you can do better...you just need to work on composition.  keep in mind, not every image is going to appeal to every viewer; the key is, though, to create images that will give people more reasons to want to look at them than to just pass them by.  and, when it comes to challenges, well, read scalvert''s thread about the recipe for ribboning...', '2005-01-15 16:22:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(1109215, 134370, 23394, '<td valign="top">interesting image, though i''m not sure i''d consider that background bokeh.  and it''s not that i''m looking for blobs of light--i''m just looking for backgrounds that enhance the subject and contribute to the image without distraction.  here, the background practically commands the image, inspite of the razor-sharp focus.</td>', 'interesting image, though i''m not sure i''d consider that background bokeh.  and it''s not that i''m looking for blobs of light--i''m just looking for backgrounds that enhance the subject and contribute to the image without distraction.  here, the background practically commands the image, inspite of the razor-sharp focus.', '2005-01-15 16:25:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(1109219, 133040, 23394, '<td valign="top">sorry if the following comes across harsh, but i call ''em as i see ''em.  this is really a bad snapshot.  the focus is on the drum, but unfortunately, you have shot from an angle doesn''t make it very interesting.  this could be done, keeping the short dof, but not from this angle.  the drummer seems to be "just there", not really doing anything.  as for the challenge, the blurriness here does not translate into bokeh.</td>', 'sorry if the following comes across harsh, but i call ''em as i see ''em.  this is really a bad snapshot.  the focus is on the drum, but unfortunately, you have shot from an angle doesn''t make it very interesting.  this could be done, keeping the short dof, but not from this angle.  the drummer seems to be "just there", not really doing anything.  as for the challenge, the blurriness here does not translate into bokeh.', '2005-01-15 16:30:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(1109223, 134732, 23394, '<td valign="top">this is an interesting shot that could be even more interesting with more detail in the drop.  on the other hand, working with droplets is a major PITA, so kudos for that.  you have achieved a nice bokeh effect, i just think that there is too, too much dead space in the image as a whole.  you could easily do without the left 25% of the image (hold your hand up to the image, and you''ll see what i mean).  it could also stand to lose a bit off the top.  aside from that, this is pleasant image.  good luck!</td>', 'this is an interesting shot that could be even more interesting with more detail in the drop.  on the other hand, working with droplets is a major PITA, so kudos for that.  you have achieved a nice bokeh effect, i just think that there is too, too much dead space in the image as a whole.  you could easily do without the left 25% of the image (hold your hand up to the image, and you''ll see what i mean).  it could also stand to lose a bit off the top.  aside from that, this is pleasant image.  good luck!', '2005-01-15 16:34:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(1109224, 134518, 23394, '<td valign="top">you have some bokeh here, but other than that, it i find the blowouts a bit overwhelming.</td>', 'you have some bokeh here, but other than that, it i find the blowouts a bit overwhelming.', '2005-01-15 16:36:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(1109227, 134646, 23394, '<td valign="top">interesting image.  i know this wasn''t easy to shoot, and you have achieved a bokeh effect.  i like how the darkness of the image feeds into the ultimate fatility.  good luck.</td>', 'interesting image.  i know this wasn''t easy to shoot, and you have achieved a bokeh effect.  i like how the darkness of the image feeds into the ultimate fatility.  good luck.', '2005-01-15 16:38:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(1109240, 134566, 23394, '<td valign="top">interesting take on the challenge.  i can''t say that this is not bokeh, but it''s not what i would have thought of.  only your final score will tell you whether or not you were too far out of the box (and then it will be up to you to decide if you want to push the envelope or if you want to chase ribbons...)  good luck!</td>', 'interesting take on the challenge.  i can''t say that this is not bokeh, but it''s not what i would have thought of.  only your final score will tell you whether or not you were too far out of the box (and then it will be up to you to decide if you want to push the envelope or if you want to chase ribbons...)  good luck!', '2005-01-15 16:44:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(1109243, 134559, 23394, '<td valign="top">ay-yi-yi.  great capture.  not sure how i feel about its bokeh with regards to the background creating a feeling.  for me, this image is all about the paw and the claw, and that is all that really gets my attention (well, that, and the two pieces of crud in the fur that you could have cloned out... ;-)).</td>', 'ay-yi-yi.  great capture.  not sure how i feel about its bokeh with regards to the background creating a feeling.  for me, this image is all about the paw and the claw, and that is all that really gets my attention (well, that, and the two pieces of crud in the fur that you could have cloned out... ;-)).', '2005-01-15 16:47:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(1109245, 133759, 23394, '<td valign="top">initially, this image pops.  as i look at it more, it seems a bit over sharpened.</td>', 'initially, this image pops.  as i look at it more, it seems a bit over sharpened.', '2005-01-15 16:48:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(1109249, 133674, 23394, '<td valign="top">and a nice portrait it is, indeed.  i think you would have had a stronger bokeh entry, though, without the other cows in the background.  they are more of a distraction away from your subject than an enhancement that supports your subject.</td>', 'and a nice portrait it is, indeed.  i think you would have had a stronger bokeh entry, though, without the other cows in the background.  they are more of a distraction away from your subject than an enhancement that supports your subject.', '2005-01-15 16:50:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(1109251, 134289, 23394, '<td valign="top">excellent capture.  i think you would have had a stronger entry, though, if you had tended to the blowouts (and, this being under advanced editing rules, there are plenty of things you could have done legally).  good luck!</td>', 'excellent capture.  i think you would have had a stronger entry, though, if you had tended to the blowouts (and, this being under advanced editing rules, there are plenty of things you could have done legally).  good luck!', '2005-01-15 16:52:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(1109254, 134630, 23394, '<td valign="top">sorry, but lens-baby effects don''t create bokeh.</td>', 'sorry, but lens-baby effects don''t create bokeh.', '2005-01-15 16:53:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(1109283, 134630, 32103, '<td valign="top">this picture is amazing...wow..i like it alot..</td>', 'this picture is amazing...wow..i like it alot..', '2005-01-15 17:30:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(1109294, 134758, 9668, '<td valign="top">Wow, that is a beaty. Nice capture of the number three, beautiful lighting, awsome shot!</td>', 'Wow, that is a beaty. Nice capture of the number three, beautiful lighting, awsome shot!', '2005-01-15 17:49:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(1109298, 134775, 9668, '<td valign="top">Nice focal point. Like the green yelllows (or yellow greens).</td>', 'Nice focal point. Like the green yelllows (or yellow greens).', '2005-01-15 18:02:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(1109354, 133779, 18838, '<td valign="top">like the idea ... nice shallow DOF, but does not give me the bokeh feeling ... i think it might have been better with focus on the foreground and a bigger continuous area of out of focus behind</td>', 'like the idea ... nice shallow DOF, but does not give me the bokeh feeling ... i think it might have been better with focus on the foreground and a bigger continuous area of out of focus behind', '2005-01-15 18:39:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(1109359, 134758, 18838, '<td valign="top">i guess people may complain that the bkg is not bokeh enough ... it is a fantastic picture though</td>', 'i guess people may complain that the bkg is not bokeh enough ... it is a fantastic picture though', '2005-01-15 18:44:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(1109363, 134146, 1024, '<td valign="top">My choice for the blue ribbon and one of only 2 tens i gave on this challenge</td>', 'My choice for the blue ribbon and one of only 2 tens i gave on this challenge', '2005-01-15 18:46:46.000000', NULL, 1),
