(1109947, 134495, 12809, '<td valign="top">I like this.  I like the selective color.  The dark bg is a nice contrast - almost life vs. death.</td>', 'I like this.  I like the selective color.  The dark bg is a nice contrast - almost life vs. death.', '2005-01-16 00:30:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(1109953, 134489, 12809, '<td valign="top">Simple but very pretty.  I like the soft cool colors.  Nice job.</td>', 'Simple but very pretty.  I like the soft cool colors.  Nice job.', '2005-01-16 00:31:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(1109960, 134807, 12809, '<td valign="top">Simple and pretty.  Good use of negative space.  I can see this as really pretty notepaper. :-)</td>', 'Simple and pretty.  Good use of negative space.  I can see this as really pretty notepaper. :-)', '2005-01-16 00:32:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(1109967, 134295, 12809, '<td valign="top">Really like the lighting.  Nice colors too.</td>', 'Really like the lighting.  Nice colors too.', '2005-01-16 00:33:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(1109977, 133849, 12809, '<td valign="top">Good bokeh but the subject is a little unappealing.</td>', 'Good bokeh but the subject is a little unappealing.', '2005-01-16 00:34:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(1109982, 134546, 12809, '<td valign="top">Those eyes!  Love the color tones of this.</td>', 'Those eyes!  Love the color tones of this.', '2005-01-16 00:35:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(1109988, 134404, 12809, '<td valign="top">I like this but it''s almost a little too dark...</td>', 'I like this but it''s almost a little too dark...', '2005-01-16 00:36:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(1110000, 134771, 12809, '<td valign="top">Nice idea and good bokeh. You even caught some motion in the drop.   My only nitpick with this is that the "blood" is too metallic looking to be real.  Not that you should use real blood...lol...but I dunno...there must be something else...?</td>', 'Nice idea and good bokeh. You even caught some motion in the drop.   My only nitpick with this is that the "blood" is too metallic looking to be real.  Not that you should use real blood...lol...but I dunno...there must be something else...?', '2005-01-16 00:37:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(1110008, 134161, 12809, '<td valign="top">I can''t even make out what this is...?  Not overly interesting subject matter, sorry.</td>', 'I can''t even make out what this is...?  Not overly interesting subject matter, sorry.', '2005-01-16 00:39:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(1110045, 134570, 30818, '<td valign="top">Wow...  That looks like a real ad for Dos Equis</td>', 'Wow...  That looks like a real ad for Dos Equis', '2005-01-16 00:54:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(1110313, 133219, 16046, '<td valign="top">Soooooo cute, well done</td>', 'Soooooo cute, well done', '2005-01-16 03:25:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(1110314, 134409, 16046, '<td valign="top">Perfect, well done</td>', 'Perfect, well done', '2005-01-16 03:26:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(1110315, 134796, 16046, '<td valign="top">very nice, well done</td>', 'very nice, well done', '2005-01-16 03:26:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(1110317, 134159, 16046, '<td valign="top">good shot, works</td>', 'good shot, works', '2005-01-16 03:27:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(1110365, 134392, 23394, '<td valign="top">you have most definitely achieved a bokeh effect, but it is rather busy.  excellent job focusing and composing of your subjects.  would have found the image stronger if the beads in the background were behind the subject and then to have cropped off the right 40% of the image.  good luck!</td>', 'you have most definitely achieved a bokeh effect, but it is rather busy.  excellent job focusing and composing of your subjects.  would have found the image stronger if the beads in the background were behind the subject and then to have cropped off the right 40% of the image.  good luck!', '2005-01-16 04:02:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(1110375, 133920, 23394, '<td valign="top">lovely colors and nice bokeh.  i''m sure this will look nice hanging on your wall.  good luck!</td>', 'lovely colors and nice bokeh.  i''m sure this will look nice hanging on your wall.  good luck!', '2005-01-16 04:06:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(1110378, 134295, 23394, '<td valign="top">yes, you have achieved a bokeh effect, but i find the foreground blurring a bit disconcerting.  i love the colors, but also have a hard time with the extreme brightness on the right.  now that you know how to get this effect, the key is to put it to work for you.  move around, changing your angle and perspective until you find a background composition that compliments your subject completely.  good luck!</td>', 'yes, you have achieved a bokeh effect, but i find the foreground blurring a bit disconcerting.  i love the colors, but also have a hard time with the extreme brightness on the right.  now that you know how to get this effect, the key is to put it to work for you.  move around, changing your angle and perspective until you find a background composition that compliments your subject completely.  good luck!', '2005-01-16 04:10:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(1110383, 134605, 23394, '<td valign="top">yes, you have achieved a bokeh effect that definitely adds a feeling to the image (albeit, not a pleasing feeling).  seeing that you know how to do this, i imagine you could recreate it using any number of objects other than a cliched chess piece...<br/></td>', 'yes, you have achieved a bokeh effect that definitely adds a feeling to the image (albeit, not a pleasing feeling).  seeing that you know how to do this, i imagine you could recreate it using any number of objects other than a cliched chess piece...', '2005-01-16 04:12:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(1110391, 134675, 23394, '<td valign="top">very interesting play on the challenge.  excellent composition and choice of colors, as well as near-great control on the lighting (i know the tiles are white, but the tops appear blown).  i am really looking forward to finding out who entered this, as this is representative of the works of only a handful of dpcers.  really expect to see this on the front page.  good luck!</td>', 'very interesting play on the challenge.  excellent composition and choice of colors, as well as near-great control on the lighting (i know the tiles are white, but the tops appear blown).  i am really looking forward to finding out who entered this, as this is representative of the works of only a handful of dpcers.  really expect to see this on the front page.  good luck!', '2005-01-16 04:17:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(1110395, 134811, 23394, '<td valign="top">while this is an interesting image, i don''t really find bokeh here.  this is more of a macro with a shallow dof.  lovely colors, though.</td>', 'while this is an interesting image, i don''t really find bokeh here.  this is more of a macro with a shallow dof.  lovely colors, though.', '2005-01-16 04:20:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(1110404, 133405, 23394, '<td valign="top">with an abstract image as this, you need an engaging subject if you are going to capture and keep the viewer''s attention.  it looks like you have all the potential for great bokeh; i can''t help but feel you would have had a stronger image if you had shot in portrait mode and included more of the subject--it really looks like it could capture the imagination.  just my opinion, of course.  good luck!</td>', 'with an abstract image as this, you need an engaging subject if you are going to capture and keep the viewer''s attention.  it looks like you have all the potential for great bokeh; i can''t help but feel you would have had a stronger image if you had shot in portrait mode and included more of the subject--it really looks like it could capture the imagination.  just my opinion, of course.  good luck!', '2005-01-16 04:22:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(1110407, 134510, 23394, '<td valign="top">excellent image, wonderful colors.  i really like the composition with the split framing.  might be a bit on the dark side for most voters, but i''m sure this will look nice hanging on your wall.  good luck!</td>', 'excellent image, wonderful colors.  i really like the composition with the split framing.  might be a bit on the dark side for most voters, but i''m sure this will look nice hanging on your wall.  good luck!', '2005-01-16 04:24:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(1110421, 133649, 17507, '<td valign="top">Lovely image, but I don''t think the background helps the image at all. It''s appropriate for the picture, but it''s a very neutral element.</td>', 'Lovely image, but I don''t think the background helps the image at all. It''s appropriate for the picture, but it''s a very neutral element.', '2005-01-16 04:29:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(1110424, 134712, 23394, '<td valign="top">i appreciate your effort here, but think you may have missed the mark.  your background, while blurry and oof, is not really enhancing your subject, and the lighting at this time of day is a bit too strong.  from a different angle with different lighting, you could produce a more pleasing image, but here, it is not really working for me.</td>', 'i appreciate your effort here, but think you may have missed the mark.  your background, while blurry and oof, is not really enhancing your subject, and the lighting at this time of day is a bit too strong.  from a different angle with different lighting, you could produce a more pleasing image, but here, it is not really working for me.', '2005-01-16 04:30:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(1110434, 134816, 23394, '<td valign="top">i appreciate your effort here, but it is really not working for me.  from the image quality, i''m going to guess that you might be asking more from your camera than it is capable of.  one thing to keep in mind before you submit to a challenge is whether or not your image is one that you would really want to hang on your wall.  while i ''like'' most of my entries, the ones that have scored higher are the ones that others would like to hang on their walls.  don''t let this discourage you; it is a weekly learning experience that only works if you keep on trying!  good luck in future entries!</td>', 'i appreciate your effort here, but it is really not working for me.  from the image quality, i''m going to guess that you might be asking more from your camera than it is capable of.  one thing to keep in mind before you submit to a challenge is whether or not your image is one that you would really want to hang on your wall.  while i ''like'' most of my entries, the ones that have scored higher are the ones that others would like to hang on their walls.  don''t let this discourage you; it is a weekly learning experience that only works if you keep on trying!  good luck in future entries!', '2005-01-16 04:35:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(1110441, 134573, 23394, '<td valign="top">aptly titled...  you have a lot of blur, but i don''t think it is really enhancing your image.  when i''m viewing images in the context of a technique, i''m not just looking for technique, but whether or not i would want to hang the image on my wall.  here, i think you have a subject with wall-hanging potential, but not the way you have presented it here.</td>', 'aptly titled...  you have a lot of blur, but i don''t think it is really enhancing your image.  when i''m viewing images in the context of a technique, i''m not just looking for technique, but whether or not i would want to hang the image on my wall.  here, i think you have a subject with wall-hanging potential, but not the way you have presented it here.', '2005-01-16 04:39:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(1110465, 133812, 23394, '<td valign="top">ok, first, you have achieved a bokeh effect, and consequently, have proven that you are capable of doing it.  now what you have to do is to harness it to put it to work for you.  here, it is a good backdrop for your subject.  the problem with the image, though, is the subject itself.<br/> <br/>the color on the handle is great.  it is eye-catching and leads into the gauge.  unfortunately, that''s where it starts to lose appeal.  the focus is a bit soft and the colors are not that engaging.  next, your eye hits the water, and it runs the eye right out the bottom of the image, rather than keeping it in the image.<br/> <br/>the keys to scoring well are nailing the challenge concept (which you did), paying attention to all the details (which you almost did), composition (needs some work), and appeal (this is a bit less than appealling, sorry).  i''d recommend two things:  1) reading and re-reading scalvert''s thread on the recipe for ribbonning (it was back around 12/30 or 12/31), and 2) before you submit an entry, ask yourself, "is this something that others would really want to hang on their walls?" or "is this an image that if someone encountered in a magazine, they would actually pause to look at it for more than a blip?"  if your honest answer is "no", then you should realistically expect a score between 4 and 5.25.<br/> <br/>no matter what, though, don''t let the scoring discourage you.  take all the comments you get, and, when possible, revisit your challenge shots and try to apply the comments.  good luck, and keep on shooting!</td>', 'ok, first, you have achieved a bokeh effect, and consequently, have proven that you are capable of doing it.  now what you have to do is to harness it to put it to work for you.  here, it is a good backdrop for your subject.  the problem with the image, though, is the subject itself. the color on the handle is great.  it is eye-catching and leads into the gauge.  unfortunately, that''s where it starts to lose appeal.  the focus is a bit soft and the colors are not that engaging.  next, your eye hits the water, and it runs the eye right out the bottom of the image, rather than keeping it in the image. the keys to scoring well are nailing the challenge concept (which you did), paying attention to all the details (which you almost did), composition (needs some work), and appeal (this is a bit less than appealling, sorry).  i''d recommend two things:  1) reading and re-reading scalvert''s thread on the recipe for ribbonning (it was back around 12/30 or 12/31), and 2) before you submit an entry, ask yourself, "is this something that others would really want to hang on their walls?" or "is this an image that if someone encountered in a magazine, they would actually pause to look at it for more than a blip?"  if your honest answer is "no", then you should realistically expect a score between 4 and 5.25. no matter what, though, don''t let the scoring discourage you.  take all the comments you get, and, when possible, revisit your challenge shots and try to apply the comments.  good luck, and keep on shooting!', '2005-01-16 04:52:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(1110474, 133694, 23394, '<td valign="top">this has something of a bokeh effect, but even with the red cup, the background is more the subject of the image.</td>', 'this has something of a bokeh effect, but even with the red cup, the background is more the subject of the image.', '2005-01-16 04:55:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(1110486, 133120, 23394, '<td valign="top">while i appreciate your effort here, your background is more of a distraction than a complimentary enhancement for your subject.  i think your image would be a lot stronger if you cropped off the right half (hold your hand up to the screen and you''ll see what i mean).</td>', 'while i appreciate your effort here, your background is more of a distraction than a complimentary enhancement for your subject.  i think your image would be a lot stronger if you cropped off the right half (hold your hand up to the screen and you''ll see what i mean).', '2005-01-16 04:57:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(1110492, 134633, 23394, '<td valign="top">while i appreciate your effort here, i am finding your background more of a distraction than a complimentary enhancement to your subject.  i think your image would be a lot stronger if you cropped off the left 30% of the image (hold your hand up to the screen to see what i mean).  the lightness leads my eye away from the subject and ultimately off the image.</td>', 'while i appreciate your effort here, i am finding your background more of a distraction than a complimentary enhancement to your subject.  i think your image would be a lot stronger if you cropped off the left 30% of the image (hold your hand up to the screen to see what i mean).  the lightness leads my eye away from the subject and ultimately off the image.', '2005-01-16 04:59:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(1110498, 134668, 23394, '<td valign="top">yes, you have bokeh, but, for me, the way it is producing a split horizon takes away from what could be an excellent image.  if you had changed perspective to have either the green or the tan as the whole background, this would have rocked.  excellent focus, lighting, choice of colors, and dof, as well as an interesting subject.  good luck!</td>', 'yes, you have bokeh, but, for me, the way it is producing a split horizon takes away from what could be an excellent image.  if you had changed perspective to have either the green or the tan as the whole background, this would have rocked.  excellent focus, lighting, choice of colors, and dof, as well as an interesting subject.  good luck!', '2005-01-16 05:02:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(1110509, 134792, 23394, '<td valign="top">this is an interesting image with good bokeh.  i appreciate how hard this must have been to capture without undue lens flare--good work.  all the diagonals make this interesting to view.  i just hope that the subdued colors aren''t too subtle to catch the viewer/voter''s attention.  you possible could have had a little more dof, as the background, not the subject matter, is what is providing your bokeh.  good luck!</td>', 'this is an interesting image with good bokeh.  i appreciate how hard this must have been to capture without undue lens flare--good work.  all the diagonals make this interesting to view.  i just hope that the subdued colors aren''t too subtle to catch the viewer/voter''s attention.  you possible could have had a little more dof, as the background, not the subject matter, is what is providing your bokeh.  good luck!', '2005-01-16 05:05:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(1110511, 134631, 23394, '<td valign="top">while i appreciate your effort, i consider this more of a macro with a shallow dof than an image with bokeh...</td>', 'while i appreciate your effort, i consider this more of a macro with a shallow dof than an image with bokeh...', '2005-01-16 05:06:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(1110523, 133775, 23394, '<td valign="top">while i appreciate your effort here, i think that it is falling a bit short.  for bokeh to work, it has to compliment and enhance the subject.  here, the skater is the dominant subject, and it is oof.  the foreground elements are just that, even though they are what is in focus.  with some judicious cropping, you actually could have pulled a strong entry out of this image (ie, if you had zeroed in on the set of leaves on the right hand side).  hope this helps.</td>', 'while i appreciate your effort here, i think that it is falling a bit short.  for bokeh to work, it has to compliment and enhance the subject.  here, the skater is the dominant subject, and it is oof.  the foreground elements are just that, even though they are what is in focus.  with some judicious cropping, you actually could have pulled a strong entry out of this image (ie, if you had zeroed in on the set of leaves on the right hand side).  hope this helps.', '2005-01-16 05:09:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(1110530, 133660, 23394, '<td valign="top">yes, you have achieved a bokeh effect, but it is more of a distraction than an enhancement for your subject.  the subject and general composition are interesting, but the amount of detail found in the background is more visual clutter than complimentary.</td>', 'yes, you have achieved a bokeh effect, but it is more of a distraction than an enhancement for your subject.  the subject and general composition are interesting, but the amount of detail found in the background is more visual clutter than complimentary.', '2005-01-16 05:11:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(1110533, 133958, 23394, '<td valign="top">while i appreciate your effort here, this is more of a macro with a shallow dof than an image with good bokeh.</td>', 'while i appreciate your effort here, this is more of a macro with a shallow dof than an image with good bokeh.', '2005-01-16 05:12:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(1110549, 134672, 23394, '<td valign="top">i can only begin to imagine what i am looking at here...  yes, you have achieved a bokeh effect, but i am not finding the subject all that engaging.</td>', 'i can only begin to imagine what i am looking at here...  yes, you have achieved a bokeh effect, but i am not finding the subject all that engaging.', '2005-01-16 05:15:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(1110559, 134245, 23394, '<td valign="top">yes, you have achieved a bokeh effect, but i don''t find that it is really enhancing your subject.  as for the subject, something about the lighting is throwing me off.  if this was shot at red rocks outside of denver, shame on you...there is such incredible backgrounds there that you surely could have found a shot that would have rocked the voters here...</td>', 'yes, you have achieved a bokeh effect, but i don''t find that it is really enhancing your subject.  as for the subject, something about the lighting is throwing me off.  if this was shot at red rocks outside of denver, shame on you...there is such incredible backgrounds there that you surely could have found a shot that would have rocked the voters here...', '2005-01-16 05:19:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(1110579, 134803, 23394, '<td valign="top">this had all the potential in the world, but i don''t think this entry is going to fare to well.  compositionally, there the subject is looking away from the negative space, which draws the eye away from all that space, which makes it basically useless.  so, to start with, you could crop off the left 40% of the image and it would be stronger.  the lighting is just a tad too strong, which is giving the image an artificial feel, almost as if this was a stuffed bird.  the dof is a bit too shallow, making the transition from the brightly lit feathers into the oof ones a bit disconcerting.  and, to top it off, even though you have achieved bokeh (in that you have a background that does enhance and compliment your subject), i imagine that it is not the type of bokeh most voters are looking for.  at this point, let me say that i hope this helps, and i wish you good luck!</td>', 'this had all the potential in the world, but i don''t think this entry is going to fare to well.  compositionally, there the subject is looking away from the negative space, which draws the eye away from all that space, which makes it basically useless.  so, to start with, you could crop off the left 40% of the image and it would be stronger.  the lighting is just a tad too strong, which is giving the image an artificial feel, almost as if this was a stuffed bird.  the dof is a bit too shallow, making the transition from the brightly lit feathers into the oof ones a bit disconcerting.  and, to top it off, even though you have achieved bokeh (in that you have a background that does enhance and compliment your subject), i imagine that it is not the type of bokeh most voters are looking for.  at this point, let me say that i hope this helps, and i wish you good luck!', '2005-01-16 05:25:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(1110583, 134563, 23394, '<td valign="top">excellent entry, all the way around.  lovely colors, detail, composition, and great bokeh.  i just hope the voters don''t kill you for not providing a more \"technical\" bokeh.  good luck!</td>', 'excellent entry, all the way around.  lovely colors, detail, composition, and great bokeh.  i just hope the voters don''t kill you for not providing a more \"technical\" bokeh.  good luck!', '2005-01-16 05:27:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(1110587, 134642, 23394, '<td valign="top">while i appreciate your effort here, i think your background is more of a distraction than an image-enhancing element.  i love the colors and basic composition, but believe that if your background had been sky and clouds only, without the mountains, this would have rocked!!  good luck.</td>', 'while i appreciate your effort here, i think your background is more of a distraction than an image-enhancing element.  i love the colors and basic composition, but believe that if your background had been sky and clouds only, without the mountains, this would have rocked!!  good luck.', '2005-01-16 05:29:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(1110591, 134701, 28750, '<td valign="top">this is the best photo in the challenge</td>', 'this is the best photo in the challenge', '2005-01-16 05:31:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(1110650, 133793, 23394, '<td valign="top">beautiful image, excellent bokeh.  i wonder, though, if this will catch with the voters...there is something about the saturization that makes it feel a tad over processed.</td>', 'beautiful image, excellent bokeh.  i wonder, though, if this will catch with the voters...there is something about the saturization that makes it feel a tad over processed.', '2005-01-16 06:11:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(1111034, 134811, 7560, '<td valign="top">This is possibly my favorite shot in this challenge. I love the composition and the color. The split in the cork is perfect, the DOF is perfect. In short a simply amazing shot.  My only, and I mean ONLY issue with the shot is not meeting the challenge. This is excellent shallow DOF, but doesn''t  say bokeh. Which is very frusterating, because I want to just 10 this shot.  I''m going to give it a 6,  and understand that I think ths is simply amazing work. It''s on my faves list now. :)</td>', 'This is possibly my favorite shot in this challenge. I love the composition and the color. The split in the cork is perfect, the DOF is perfect. In short a simply amazing shot.  My only, and I mean ONLY issue with the shot is not meeting the challenge. This is excellent shallow DOF, but doesn''t  say bokeh. Which is very frusterating, because I want to just 10 this shot.  I''m going to give it a 6,  and understand that I think ths is simply amazing work. It''s on my faves list now. :)', '2005-01-16 09:34:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(1111232, 134713, 12809, '<td valign="top">I don''t consider this bokeh.  To me, neither the head or stars are blurred.  I find the stars distracting, actually.</td>', 'I don''t consider this bokeh.  To me, neither the head or stars are blurred.  I find the stars distracting, actually.', '2005-01-16 11:25:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(1111237, 134597, 12809, '<td valign="top">Primary colors?  I''m seeing brown, blue, neon green, and red...and a funky coloring on the bottom side of the petals.  I don''t care for this at all...</td>', 'Primary colors?  I''m seeing brown, blue, neon green, and red...and a funky coloring on the bottom side of the petals.  I don''t care for this at all...', '2005-01-16 11:28:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(1111239, 134150, 12809, '<td valign="top">Too dark for me.</td>', 'Too dark for me.', '2005-01-16 11:29:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(1111240, 134472, 12253, '<td valign="top">Nice bokeh and good color contrast.  Good capture of the flower, though light on the flower itself could be more dynamic.  However, IMHO the biggest improvement here would come from a different crop--the vertical crop, tight around the flower, shows off the bokeh but doesn''t do justice to the flower.  Bokeh is supposed to enhance the foreground, make it pop, and thus should sit in the background serving to contrast but not drawing attention to itself.</td>', 'Nice bokeh and good color contrast.  Good capture of the flower, though light on the flower itself could be more dynamic.  However, IMHO the biggest improvement here would come from a different crop--the vertical crop, tight around the flower, shows off the bokeh but doesn''t do justice to the flower.  Bokeh is supposed to enhance the foreground, make it pop, and thus should sit in the background serving to contrast but not drawing attention to itself.', '2005-01-16 11:29:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(1111242, 134127, 12809, '<td valign="top">It seems the enter image is a blur.  My understanding is that bokeh is the blur of either the fg or bg.  I don''t see that here.</td>', 'It seems the enter image is a blur.  My understanding is that bokeh is the blur of either the fg or bg.  I don''t see that here.', '2005-01-16 11:30:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(1111247, 134370, 30843, '<td valign="top">love it</td>', 'love it', '2005-01-16 11:32:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(1111249, 134812, 12253, '<td valign="top">Good use of bokeh to highlight the drop.  However, the bright background  does steal attention from the subject rather than serving only to make it stand out.</td>', 'Good use of bokeh to highlight the drop.  However, the bright background  does steal attention from the subject rather than serving only to make it stand out.', '2005-01-16 11:33:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(1111252, 134758, 30843, '<td valign="top">love it<br/></td>', 'love it', '2005-01-16 11:35:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(1111254, 134650, 12253, '<td valign="top">Very cute shot and good use of background blur.</td>', 'Very cute shot and good use of background blur.', '2005-01-16 11:35:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(1111255, 134409, 12809, '<td valign="top">You have the right idea about bokeh but I think your dof is too shallow.  Because of the pacifier we know that it is a baby in the bg, but if you look at the baby only its a bit hard to make out what it is.</td>', 'You have the right idea about bokeh but I think your dof is too shallow.  Because of the pacifier we know that it is a baby in the bg, but if you look at the baby only its a bit hard to make out what it is.', '2005-01-16 11:35:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(1111257, 134734, 12253, '<td valign="top">Excellent capture of this dog and freat use of background bokeh to make this dog stand out!  Second review, bumping up.</td>', 'Excellent capture of this dog and freat use of background bokeh to make this dog stand out!  Second review, bumping up.', '2005-01-16 11:35:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(1111262, 134704, 12253, '<td valign="top">Great shot and good use of bokeh to make the subject stand out.   It might have been a bit better if the lighter branches in the backgound didn''t stand out as much, but short of editing, I''m not sure what you could have done to prevent this.</td>', 'Great shot and good use of bokeh to make the subject stand out.   It might have been a bit better if the lighter branches in the backgound didn''t stand out as much, but short of editing, I''m not sure what you could have done to prevent this.', '2005-01-16 11:37:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(1111263, 134605, 30843, '<td valign="top">love it</td>', 'love it', '2005-01-16 11:37:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(1111269, 134283, 12253, '<td valign="top">Great shot and good use of bokeh to make the subject stand out.   The white flower is difficult to capture and you did it pretty well, except for a few small areas.</td>', 'Great shot and good use of bokeh to make the subject stand out.   The white flower is difficult to capture and you did it pretty well, except for a few small areas.', '2005-01-16 11:38:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(1111306, 134462, 12809, '<td valign="top">The idea is alright and the bokeh seems to be there but overall I don''t care for this.  It''s very grainy and pixelated (could be from upload though), the pink rose clashes with the red shoes, and the rose seems to be...unhealthy; the leaves, especially, look diseased or something.</td>', 'The idea is alright and the bokeh seems to be there but overall I don''t care for this.  It''s very grainy and pixelated (could be from upload though), the pink rose clashes with the red shoes, and the rose seems to be...unhealthy; the leaves, especially, look diseased or something.', '2005-01-16 11:54:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(1111313, 134644, 24674, '<td valign="top">needs more fg space</td>', 'needs more fg space', '2005-01-16 11:56:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(1111866, 134774, 30818, '<td valign="top">image is a little small</td>', 'image is a little small', '2005-01-16 15:08:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(1111992, 134775, 22479, '<td valign="top">While the bee is not in an ideal position (slightly behind the flower), the bokeh in this shot is magnificient! This is what the challenge is all about, well done.</td>', 'While the bee is not in an ideal position (slightly behind the flower), the bokeh in this shot is magnificient! This is what the challenge is all about, well done.', '2005-01-16 15:58:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(1112001, 134159, 22479, '<td valign="top">I like how the blades of grass silhouette in the nicely blurred backdrop. Some may point out that the immediate background grass is not quite blurred enough. I think this picture is fine exactly the way it is, and wouldn''t recommend changing anything. Well done.</td>', 'I like how the blades of grass silhouette in the nicely blurred backdrop. Some may point out that the immediate background grass is not quite blurred enough. I think this picture is fine exactly the way it is, and wouldn''t recommend changing anything. Well done.', '2005-01-16 16:01:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(1112009, 133793, 22479, '<td valign="top">Very pleasing bokeh. Would have liked the lower left orchid within the DOF, but overall well done.</td>', 'Very pleasing bokeh. Would have liked the lower left orchid within the DOF, but overall well done.', '2005-01-16 16:03:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(1112015, 134404, 22479, '<td valign="top">Quite simple and elegant. Here''s a great example of how the bokeh enhances the foreground as evidenced by the flowers in bloom within the background. Well done.</td>', 'Quite simple and elegant. Here''s a great example of how the bokeh enhances the foreground as evidenced by the flowers in bloom within the background. Well done.', '2005-01-16 16:04:20.000000', NULL, 1),
