(1113273, 134734, 25232, '<td valign="top">Thank you all for your votes and comments. This was my first entry and am pleased with the response. <br/> <br/>This shot was taken at sunset on the last day of submission. That day was the first sunny day we had had in a week so. I sat in a blind with a tele all afternoon. No luck. No birds showed up. Not one. So as a last ditch I grabbed up one of my dogs and drove down the road to a place where the sun had not yet gone behind the trees and took the shot.  <br/> <br/>On retrospect I would have to say that the members who said the picture should have been cropped tighter you are definatly on target. I tried a tighter crop later that night and it was a vast improvement. As far as improving the bokeh, sorry, that is what I was aiming for and am well pleased with the results.<br/> <br/>By the way, the background is actually trees. Green trees. The color cast of the sunset gave them the warm glow. This effect was not done in PS.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-01-17 04:20:04.</i></td>', 'Thank you all for your votes and comments. This was my first entry and am pleased with the response.  This shot was taken at sunset on the last day of submission. That day was the first sunny day we had had in a week so. I sat in a blind with a tele all afternoon. No luck. No birds showed up. Not one. So as a last ditch I grabbed up one of my dogs and drove down the road to a place where the sun had not yet gone behind the trees and took the shot.   On retrospect I would have to say that the members who said the picture should have been cropped tighter you are definatly on target. I tried a tighter crop later that night and it was a vast improvement. As far as improving the bokeh, sorry, that is what I was aiming for and am well pleased with the results. By the way, the background is actually trees. Green trees. The color cast of the sunset gave them the warm glow. This effect was not done in PS.', '2005-01-17 00:25:12.000000', '2005-01-17 04:20:04.000000', 0),
