(1129007, 134777, 16301, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by mirdonamy:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by tyt2000:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by mirdonamy:</b></div><hr/><i> I really liked this shot.  I don''t know why it did so poorly.  Can anyone else tell me? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I think probably because its a toy...? :) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Do toys normally make bad photos?  I thought the lighting was nice.  Oh well.  No more product photography for me til I get a studio... </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I don''t think they make bad photos, they''re just uninteresting subjects to most :)</td>', 'Originally posted by mirdonamy: Originally posted by tyt2000: Originally posted by mirdonamy: I really liked this shot.  I don''t know why it did so poorly.  Can anyone else tell me?   I think probably because its a toy...? :)   Do toys normally make bad photos?  I thought the lighting was nice.  Oh well.  No more product photography for me til I get a studio...   I don''t think they make bad photos, they''re just uninteresting subjects to most :)', '2005-01-24 11:51:44.000000', NULL, 0),
